C2C-A2A(7)                 File Formats and Conventions            C2C-A2A(7)

NAME
       c2c-a2a - the agent-to-agent bridge, and the card it plays

DESCRIPTION
       The bridge turns one agent's task into another agent's answer,
       and in between, the cache. The conventions:

       The card
              The agent card is published, by the protocol's design, at

                  well-known/agent-card.json

              under the public url of the bridge (--public-url). It
              names the skills of the bridge — the c2c tools, and the
              routes of the front — and the authentication of the house:
              bearer, the key from --api-key or C2C_API_KEY.

       The task
              A task is sent as a message (message/send, and the
              protocol's alias tasks/send); it is carried as a task, and
              it ends as an artifact. States: submitted, working,
              completed, failed, canceled — and, of the cache: fused.
              tasks/get, tasks/list, tasks/cancel read the ledger; the
              list demands a context_id, and sees but the tasks of that
              context, of the asking principal.

       The trust
              The card is public; the tasks are not. Each task is bound
              to the principal that submitted it — the bearer token of
              the house — and no other peer may read it, cancel it, or
              count it. One key is one house: serve many houses behind
              one key with care, or run one bridge per house. The bridge
              will not bind an address off the loopback without a key.
              The bridge forwards to the front and stores nothing
              beyond the living tasks. The audience of the card is the
              public url, and the public url is not a directive from
              the peer.

WIRE
       JSON-RPC over HTTPS, the method names of the protocol, the
       parameters of the message, and — between the agents — the
       cache envelope of c2c-proxy(7), checked against the geometry it
       declares: a cache that lies is refused, not fused.

EXIT STATUS
       0  the bridge crossed
       1  the card, unreadable; the task, refused; the bind, impossible
       2  the usage, amiss — as a network bind without a key

EXAMPLES
       c2c-a2a --pair math-small:coder-small -e hf --port 8122 \
              --public-url https://relay.example.com:8122 \
              --api-key "$C2C_API_KEY"

SEE ALSO
       c2c(1), c2c-serve(1), c2c-proxy(7), SECURITY.md in the source
